              "line": 89,
              "text": "I created these textures for dramatic visual effect. The effect will faulter as you fly close to them. There is a fix...dont fly so freaking close to mountains! That is why the original textures tend to be uniform but for me that means boring. If you think you can do better then give it a go. I created these on GIMP with photos of a small cliff. It works on the same principle as fractals. In nature the same patterns reoccur as you zoom in. Mountains out of mole hills. The same can be done with vegitation or any other natural object, even some manmade. These mountain textures can make dogfighting and racing very disorientating. It makes it challenging and gives it a real sense of speed when wizzing by the detail. Dont loose track where the peaks begin and end."
